-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura p-adic Galois lattice for the weight-two Hecke ring
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ and $p$ a prime, and write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeRingH M H 2`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L37) for the subring of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$ generated by the operators `heckeGenH` attached to the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) with $S=\emptyset$, namely `heckeTLinH` for each prime $\ell\nmid M$, `heckeULinH` for each prime $q\mid M$ and `diamondLinH` for each $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ (here $\Gamma_H(M)\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ is the image in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of the preimage of $H$ under reduction of the lower-right entry). The assertion is that there exist a type $A$ with an abelian group structure and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module structure making it finite and free over $\mathbb{Z}_p$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{T}\to\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}(A)$ and a multiplicative map $\rho$ from the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}(A)$, such that: (1) if $\varphi(t)$ lies in $p\cdot\Lambda$, where $\Lambda$ is the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-submodule of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}(A)$ spanned by the range of $\varphi$, then $t=p\,t'$ for some $t'\in\mathbb{T}$; (2) $\rho(\sigma)\varphi(t)=\varphi(t)\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ and all $t\in\mathbb{T}$; (3) for every $d\in\mathbb{N}$ there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)a-a\in p^{d}A$ for all $a\in A$; and (4) for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\neq p$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\varphi(T_\ell)\rho(\sigma)=\varphi(\langle\ell\rangle)\rho(\sigma)^2+\ell\cdot\mathrm{id}_A$, where $T_\ell$ and $\langle\ell\rangle$ denote the elements of $\mathbb{T}$ given by `heckeGenH` applied to `Gen.T ℓ` and to `Gen.dia` of the unit $\ell\bmod M$.
--
--   This packages the $p$-adic Galois representation carried by the Tate module of the Jacobian $J_H(M)$ of $X_H(M)$, together with its commuting action of the weight-two Hecke ring of level $\Gamma_H(M)$, its continuity in the form of trivial action modulo $p^d$ after a finite extension, a mod-$p$ faithfulness property of the Hecke action, and the Eichler–Shimura congruence relation $\langle\ell\rangle F^2-T_\ell F+\ell=0$ at Frobenius elements away from $Mp$. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_twoCuspEigenspace_two_le_twoCuspEigenspace_empty_of_finset`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_twoCuspEigenspace_two_le_twoCuspEigenspace_empty_of_finset) in the comparison of Hecke eigenspaces at different levels.
